# Environment variables this monorepo reads. Copy to `.env` or export them; none are required.
#
# Every agent works keyless out of the box. The two variables below are the only ones that change
# what a feed will give you; the rest tune timeouts and User-Agents.

# --- credentials (optional) -------------------------------------------------

# A free NASA key from https://api.nasa.gov/. Without it the `apod` agent uses DEMO_KEY, which
# NASA rate-limits by address (30 requests an hour, 50 a day). A key raises those limits.
NASA_API_KEY=

# SEC asks every caller to send a product name and a contact address, and refuses some callers
# with a 403 when they do not. The `company` agent sends `awesome-acps-company/1.0 (contact: see
# the repository README)` by default; put your own name and address here if SEC refuses you.
# Example: SEC_USER_AGENT=my-tool/1.0 (me@example.com)
SEC_USER_AGENT=

# --- per-agent tuning -------------------------------------------------------
#
# Each agent follows the same three-variable pattern, so the names are predictable:
#
#   <AGENT>_HTTP_TIMEOUT   seconds to wait for a feed (default 25-30)
#   <AGENT>_USER_AGENT     the User-Agent that agent sends (some feeds require a real one)
#   <AGENT>_CACHE_TTL      seconds a lookup is reused (only agents that cache)
#
# AGENT is the directory name in upper case: APOD_*, ATTACH_* (no feed, so no variables),
# COMPANY is SEC_*, FLIGHTS_*, TRIALS_*, plus the older AIR_*, ART_*, STOCKS_* and the rest.
# Naming the variables explicitly:

SEC_HTTP_TIMEOUT=
SEC_CACHE_TTL=
APOD_HTTP_TIMEOUT=
APOD_USER_AGENT=
FLIGHTS_HTTP_TIMEOUT=
FLIGHTS_USER_AGENT=
TRIALS_HTTP_TIMEOUT=
TRIALS_USER_AGENT=

# --- tools ------------------------------------------------------------------

# `tools/probe_all.py` skips the a2a_bridge probe unless this points at a running A2A server.
# Example: ACP_A2A_ENDPOINTS=nyc311=http://127.0.0.1:8787
ACP_A2A_ENDPOINTS=
